hey boys and girls i'm tim ferriss i  would like to tell you about hrv  training that stands for heart rate  variability training i  was not a participant  in hrv training i didn't use it myself  for a very long time it was recommended  initially  by josh waitzkin who's a friend of mine  he is very well known  as a world-class chess player he's also  a black belt  brazilian jiu jitsu under fina nine time  world champion marcelo garcia  and he's currently working on many other  crafts also happens to be a world  champion  in tai chi push hands so he understands  a thing or two about high performance  he also works with a lot of the best  performing investors in the finance  world  they all use hrv why so let me take a  step back we often think about  changing how we feel changing our  physiology by changing our content  so can we go to therapy and  talk ask questions be asked questions  such that  we change the stories in our minds so  that that changes how we respond to  things which changes how we feel  and voila we have increased well-being  now  that is not a bad approach but it is one  tool  another tool and another approach and  another paradigm  is to say maybe we can move in the  opposite direction so we change our  physiology and by changing our  physiology  we change how we feel and that changes  the content  all right this is actually really  important to grasp  so in other words you're working from  the body to the mind as opposed to the  mind to the body and i believe that both  can be really effective  athletes use hrv all the time the tools  that i have used  first are elite hrv i believe it's  called  it is effectively a pulse oximeter so  you clip it onto your finger  and i use that for calibrating the  morning resting  hrv then i use the aura ring which i  don't have on right now i actually use  it exclusively for sleep  o-u-r-a or a-ring which is  one of the better devices for tracking  sleep quality and hrv  and the woman i have worked with most  closely with respect to hrv is dr leah  lagos l-e-a-h-l-a-g-o-s  and she has a book on the subject so if  you search her name on amazon or  elsewhere you will find  this book and really more than anything  else because this is a set of tools  and this is one approach to working with  physiology to change how you feel to  change content  is to emphasize and really what i would  like to emphasize  is that when there's a problem very  often you'll be given a process that  moves from a to z  but sometimes if you're trying to get to  the middle somewhere you can also work  from z  to a and that is what hrv allows you  to do now the benefits that i've  experienced initially were  tremendous i saw it very quickly within  a week or so instead of it taking say  30 minutes to 90 minutes for me to fall  asleep i have a lot of  onset insomnia i was falling asleep  within  10 to 20 minutes of laying down after  doing  brief hrv training for 20 minutes  right before bed and i used an app i  believe it's called breath or breathe  there are many you can use  ultimately by using leah's book and  their other resources online  you will determine breathing sequences  that you can use to achieve a certain  degree of resonance  and we can get into the vagus nerve and  all sorts of things but there's certain  breathing patterns you can use  to change your cardiac response in my  case  there's a certain number of seconds of  inhale and  exhale you set those parameters in the  app you press go  you do it for 20 minutes and that is it  it's it's a very simple practice i was  doing it twice a day  and i encourage you guys to check it out  enjoy  you
 

